WEBVTT

00:02.425 --> 00:03.968
KATARA: Water...

00:04.802 --> 00:05.929
Earth...

00:06.679 --> 00:08.181
Fire...

00:09.015 --> 00:10.350
Air.

00:11.226 --> 00:15.271
Long ago, the four nations
lived together in harmony.

00:15.355 --> 00:18.691
Then, everything changed
when the Fire Nation attacked.

00:19.609 --> 00:22.612
Only the Avatar,
master of all four elements,

00:22.695 --> 00:23.738
could stop them.

00:23.821 --> 00:25.615
But when the world
needed him most,

00:25.698 --> 00:26.741
He vanished.

00:27.200 --> 00:28.409
100 years passed,

00:28.493 --> 00:30.995
and my brother and I
discovered the new Avatar―

00:31.079 --> 00:32.455
An airbender named Aang.

00:32.997 --> 00:35.124
And although his airbending
skills are great,

00:35.208 --> 00:37.794
he has a lot to learn before
he's ready to save anyone.

00:37.877 --> 00:39.003
AANG: Oof!

00:39.087 --> 00:42.048
But I believe Aang can save the world.

01:00.904 --> 01:01.988
I can't believe it.

01:02.072 --> 01:03.865
I know the war has spread far,

01:03.949 --> 01:06.034
but Omashu always seemed...

01:06.117 --> 01:07.410
Untouchable.

01:07.702 --> 01:09.412
Up until now, it was.

01:09.746 --> 01:13.166
Now, Ba Sing Se is the only great
Earth Kingdom stronghold left.

01:13.500 --> 01:14.876
KATARA: This is horrible.

01:15.877 --> 01:17.837
But we have to move on.

01:17.963 --> 01:18.964
No.

01:19.089 --> 01:20.799
I'm going in to find Bumi.

01:20.924 --> 01:22.092
SOKKA: Aang, stop!

01:22.217 --> 01:24.511
We don't even know if Bumi's still...

01:24.636 --> 01:26.846
What? If he's still what?

01:27.305 --> 01:28.306
Around.

01:28.890 --> 01:31.101
I know you had
your heart set on Bumi,

01:31.184 --> 01:33.937
but there are other people
who can teach you earthbending.

01:34.020 --> 01:35.981
This isn't about
finding a teacher.

01:36.314 --> 01:37.816
This is about
finding my friend.

01:42.946 --> 01:44.614
( GROWLING )

01:45.073 --> 01:46.283
SOKKA: A secret passage?

01:46.491 --> 01:48.785
Why didn't we just
use this last time?

01:49.077 --> 01:50.412
Ugh!

01:50.495 --> 01:51.955
Does that answer
your question?

01:53.665 --> 01:54.666
Ew!

02:00.588 --> 02:02.590
( RETCHING )

02:14.811 --> 02:16.354
That wasn't as bad as I thought.

02:22.068 --> 02:23.486
( SCREAMING )

02:27.490 --> 02:29.034
Aagh!

02:29.409 --> 02:30.702
They won't let go!

02:30.785 --> 02:31.786
Help!

02:31.870 --> 02:32.871
( GRUNTING )

02:33.121 --> 02:34.497
Stop making so much noise.

02:34.706 --> 02:36.249
It's just a purple pentapus.

02:37.125 --> 02:39.044
( GROANING )

02:40.920 --> 02:41.963
Oh.

02:47.677 --> 02:48.845
MAN: Hey!

02:52.015 --> 02:53.933
What are you kids
doing out past curfew?

02:54.684 --> 02:55.769
KATARA: Sorry.

02:55.852 --> 02:57.228
We were just
on our way home.

03:00.357 --> 03:01.358
Wait.

03:01.441 --> 03:02.942
What's the matter with him?

03:03.026 --> 03:04.027
Uh...

03:04.110 --> 03:05.987
He has pentapox, sir.

03:07.906 --> 03:10.700
Um, it's highly contagious.

03:12.452 --> 03:13.620
( GROANING )

03:13.703 --> 03:16.164
It's so awful! I'm dying!

03:16.373 --> 03:17.415
KATARA: And deadly.

03:17.499 --> 03:20.085
Hey, I think I've heard of pentapox.

03:20.168 --> 03:22.003
Didn't your cousin Chang die of it?

03:22.087 --> 03:23.630
We better go wash our hands.

03:23.713 --> 03:24.798
And burn our clothes.

03:24.881 --> 03:26.299
( COUGHING )

03:27.092 --> 03:28.802
Thank you, sewer friend!

03:32.680 --> 03:34.891
WOMAN: When tracking
your brother and uncle,

03:34.974 --> 03:36.601
traveling with
the royal procession

03:36.684 --> 03:38.895
may no longer be an option.

03:39.145 --> 03:41.022
May no longer be wise.

03:41.106 --> 03:44.317
BOTH: If you hope to keep
the element of surprise.

03:44.401 --> 03:45.610
AZULA: You're right.

03:45.693 --> 03:47.445
The royal procession is dead weight.

03:47.529 --> 03:49.030
If I want to catch my prey,

03:49.114 --> 03:51.074
I must be agile, nimble.

03:51.366 --> 03:53.660
I need a small, elite team.

03:54.035 --> 03:56.913
It's time to visit some old friends.

04:07.841 --> 04:09.926
KATARA: Let's find Bumi
and get out of here.

04:10.009 --> 04:11.719
Where would they
be keeping him?

04:11.803 --> 04:14.347
Somewhere he can't earthbend.

04:14.431 --> 04:16.141
Somewhere made of metal.

04:22.730 --> 04:24.482
There really is no fathoming

04:24.566 --> 04:25.733
the depths of my hatred

04:25.817 --> 04:27.318
for this place.

04:27.527 --> 04:30.071
Mai, your father was appointed governor.

04:30.447 --> 04:32.115
We're like royalty here.

04:32.198 --> 04:34.033
Be happy and enjoy it.

04:38.037 --> 04:39.747
MAN: The targets are approaching.

04:39.831 --> 04:41.124
Take them out.

04:41.583 --> 04:44.419
I thought my life was
boring in the Fire Nation,

04:44.502 --> 04:47.046
but this place is unbearably bleak.

04:47.297 --> 04:49.299
Nothing ever happens.

04:54.095 --> 04:55.597
( RUMBLING )

05:04.314 --> 05:05.523
The resistance!

05:13.865 --> 05:15.783
( GRUNTING )

05:35.303 --> 05:36.846
( YELLS )

05:38.264 --> 05:39.349
( SIGHS )

05:51.986 --> 05:52.987
Ty Lee,

05:53.071 --> 05:54.656
could that possibly be you?

05:56.074 --> 05:57.242
Azula!

06:01.120 --> 06:03.706
It is so good to see you!

06:03.957 --> 06:06.167
Please, don't let me interrupt your...

06:06.251 --> 06:08.002
Whatever it is you were doing.

06:08.795 --> 06:09.963
Tell me...

06:10.046 --> 06:12.507
What is the daughter of a nobleman
doing here?

06:12.590 --> 06:14.342
Certainly our parents didn't send us

06:14.425 --> 06:16.177
to the Royal Fire Academy for Girls

06:16.261 --> 06:18.596
to end up in places like this.

06:21.641 --> 06:23.601
I have a proposition for you.

06:23.685 --> 06:24.936
I'm hunting a traitor.

06:25.228 --> 06:27.146
You remember my old fuddy-duddy uncle,

06:27.230 --> 06:28.231
don't you?

06:28.565 --> 06:30.984
Oh, yeah. He was so funny.

06:32.110 --> 06:34.862
I would be honored
if you would join me on my mission.

06:34.988 --> 06:36.281
Oh, I, uh...

06:36.364 --> 06:37.699
Would love to.

06:38.908 --> 06:39.951
But the truth is

06:40.034 --> 06:41.911
I'm really happy here.

06:41.995 --> 06:44.706
I mean, my aura has never been pinker.

06:45.081 --> 06:47.125
I'll take your word for it.

06:47.208 --> 06:48.960
Well, I wouldn't want you to give up

06:49.043 --> 06:51.462
the life you love just to please me.

06:52.338 --> 06:54.048
Thank you, Azula.

06:55.300 --> 06:56.968
Of course, before I leave,

06:57.051 --> 06:58.803
I'm going to catch your show.

06:58.886 --> 06:59.887
( GASPS )

06:59.971 --> 07:01.973
Uh, yeah, sure.

07:02.056 --> 07:03.141
Of course.

07:05.935 --> 07:08.563
AANG: So, is King Bumi with you guys?

07:09.105 --> 07:10.648
Is he leading the resistance?

07:11.024 --> 07:12.233
Of course not.

07:12.567 --> 07:13.776
The day of the invasion,

07:13.860 --> 07:15.570
we readied ourselves for battle.

07:15.653 --> 07:17.572
We were prepared to defend our city,

07:17.655 --> 07:19.824
To fight for our lives
and for our freedom.

07:20.325 --> 07:22.869
But before we even had a chance,

07:22.952 --> 07:25.830
King Bumi surrendered.

07:33.463 --> 07:34.922
The day of the invasion,

07:35.006 --> 07:36.841
I asked King Bumi
what he wanted to do.

07:37.258 --> 07:38.926
He looked me
in the eye and said...

07:40.887 --> 07:42.847
I'm going to do nothing.

07:42.930 --> 07:43.931
Ha ha ha ha!

07:44.015 --> 07:45.308
( SNORT ) Ha ha ha.

07:46.100 --> 07:47.310
It doesn't matter now.

07:47.602 --> 07:48.770
Fighting the Fire Nation

07:48.853 --> 07:50.188
is the only path to freedom.

07:50.563 --> 07:53.024
And freedom is worth dying for.

07:53.816 --> 07:55.818
Actually, there's another path to freedom.

07:55.902 --> 07:57.403
You could leave Omashu.

07:57.654 --> 07:59.280
You're directing all your energy

07:59.364 --> 08:00.573
to fight the Fire Nation,

08:00.823 --> 08:02.950
But you're outnumbered.
You can't win.

08:03.660 --> 08:05.036
Now is the time to retreat

08:05.119 --> 08:06.913
so you can live to fight another day.

08:07.246 --> 08:08.706
You don't understand.

08:08.790 --> 08:09.999
They've taken our home,

08:10.083 --> 08:12.377
and we have to fight them at any cost!

08:12.460 --> 08:13.628
I don't know, Yalo.

08:13.711 --> 08:15.046
Living to fight another day

08:15.129 --> 08:17.256
is starting to sound
pretty good to me.

08:17.465 --> 08:19.050
Yeah, I'm with the kid.

08:19.676 --> 08:20.802
( PEOPLE MURMURING )

08:24.180 --> 08:25.264
Fine.

08:25.348 --> 08:27.850
But there's thousands of citizens
that need to leave.

08:27.934 --> 08:29.602
How are we gonna get them all out?

08:29.686 --> 08:30.687
Suckers!

08:30.770 --> 08:31.854
( COOING )

08:32.730 --> 08:35.733
You're all about to come down
with a nasty case of pentapox.

08:48.621 --> 08:49.622
( GRUNTING )

08:52.750 --> 08:54.502
SOKKA: The marks make you look sick,

08:54.585 --> 08:55.962
but you gotta act sick, too!

08:56.379 --> 08:57.505
You gotta sell it.

08:58.214 --> 09:00.091
( GROANING )

09:03.553 --> 09:05.221
Now, that's what I'm talking about.

09:05.638 --> 09:07.265
Years of practice.

09:08.975 --> 09:10.059
Ok, everyone,

09:10.143 --> 09:11.269
into sick formation!

09:12.353 --> 09:13.521
( COOING )

09:13.604 --> 09:14.814
Aang, what are you doing?

09:14.897 --> 09:16.357
Aren't you coming with us?

09:16.441 --> 09:18.943
No. I'm not leaving until I find Bumi.

09:21.738 --> 09:23.823
Sorry, Momo. I'll feed you later.

09:30.496 --> 09:33.166
( PEOPLE GROANING )

09:50.141 --> 09:51.976
Plague! Plague!

09:53.269 --> 09:54.395
( CLANGING )

09:59.734 --> 10:01.527
What is going on down there?!

10:01.611 --> 10:02.820
I saw some kids yesterday

10:02.904 --> 10:04.322
who were sick with pentapox.

10:04.405 --> 10:05.490
It must have spread.

10:05.573 --> 10:06.824
Pentapox!

10:07.074 --> 10:09.243
Hmm. I'm pretty sure
I've heard of that.

10:09.952 --> 10:11.496
WOMAN: Oh, this is terrible.

10:11.579 --> 10:12.789
GUARD: What should we do?

10:12.872 --> 10:14.665
GOVERNOR: Drive them out of the city,

10:14.749 --> 10:16.125
but don't touch them.

10:16.209 --> 10:18.628
We have to rid the city of this disease.

10:20.505 --> 10:22.131
Fire flakes, dad?

10:22.757 --> 10:24.133
( GASPS )

10:24.217 --> 10:25.301
How awful!

10:36.395 --> 10:37.396
( PANTING )

10:37.480 --> 10:38.564
Flopsie!

10:52.411 --> 10:53.412
( CHUCKLES )

10:53.496 --> 10:54.705
Come on, Flopsie.

10:54.789 --> 10:56.123
You gotta help me find Bumi.

10:56.207 --> 10:57.291
Yip, yip!

10:58.584 --> 11:01.254
Oh, I guess that
doesn't work with you.

11:01.337 --> 11:02.505
Let's go.

11:06.592 --> 11:08.135
( COOING )

11:10.847 --> 11:12.807
( BABY GIGGLING )

11:17.937 --> 11:19.689
( CHITTERING )

11:28.781 --> 11:30.324
( GIGGLING )

11:38.457 --> 11:40.126
Whoa!

11:51.804 --> 11:53.097
Wee!

12:01.355 --> 12:02.982
( CHITTERING )

12:03.774 --> 12:06.152
( PEOPLE GROANING )

12:15.494 --> 12:17.163
We're deeply honored

12:17.246 --> 12:18.789
to have the Fire Lord's daughter

12:18.873 --> 12:20.374
at our humble circus.

12:20.917 --> 12:22.418
And tell us if there's anything

12:22.501 --> 12:25.046
we can do to make
the show more enjoyable.

12:25.129 --> 12:26.172
I will.

12:32.929 --> 12:34.138
Incredible.

12:34.555 --> 12:35.806
Do you think she'll fall?

12:35.890 --> 12:37.058
Of course not.

12:37.141 --> 12:39.101
Then wouldn't it make it more interesting

12:39.185 --> 12:40.686
if you removed the net?

12:41.270 --> 12:43.105
Uh, the thing is...

12:43.189 --> 12:44.190
The performers―

12:44.273 --> 12:45.775
You're right. You're right.

12:45.858 --> 12:46.984
That's been done.

12:48.945 --> 12:50.029
I know.

12:50.112 --> 12:51.781
Set the net on fire.

12:51.864 --> 12:53.449
Of course, Princess.

13:01.666 --> 13:03.626
Brilliant. Just brilliant.

13:03.709 --> 13:04.919
Ooh!

13:05.002 --> 13:07.254
What kind of dangerous animals
do you have?

13:07.338 --> 13:10.216
Well, our circus boasts
the most exotic assortment―

13:10.299 --> 13:11.425
Release them all!

13:13.928 --> 13:15.054
( ELEPHANT TRUMPETS )

13:15.137 --> 13:16.555
( TIGER ROARS )

13:25.398 --> 13:26.941
We looked everywhere.

13:27.024 --> 13:28.651
No Bumi.

13:28.734 --> 13:30.403
( MOANS )

13:31.821 --> 13:33.114
MAN: We've got a problem.

13:33.197 --> 13:34.407
We just did a head count.

13:34.949 --> 13:37.201
KATARA: Oh, no.
Did someone get left behind?

13:37.743 --> 13:39.578
No. We have an extra.

13:45.751 --> 13:47.586
( WEEPING )

13:49.255 --> 13:52.633
GOVERNOR: So, the resistance
has kidnapped my son.

13:52.717 --> 13:55.469
Everything is so clever, so tricky―

13:55.553 --> 13:57.513
Just like their King Bumi.

13:57.596 --> 13:58.931
What do you want to do, sir?

14:05.438 --> 14:07.356
What an exquisite performance.

14:07.440 --> 14:08.566
I can't wait to see

14:08.649 --> 14:10.234
how you'll top yourself tomorrow.

14:10.443 --> 14:11.444
I'm sorry, Azula,

14:11.527 --> 14:13.988
but unfortunately there
won't be a show tomorrow.

14:14.071 --> 14:15.114
Really?

14:15.781 --> 14:17.908
The universe is giving
me strong hints

14:17.992 --> 14:19.702
that it's time for a career change.

14:20.578 --> 14:22.246
I want to join you on your mission.

14:28.586 --> 14:29.587
( COOING )

14:34.050 --> 14:36.177
No! Bad Fire Nation baby.

14:36.552 --> 14:38.304
Waah!

14:39.930 --> 14:41.140
Oh, all right.

14:43.017 --> 14:44.935
( COOING )

14:46.020 --> 14:47.772
Oh, you're so cute!

14:47.855 --> 14:48.856
Ooh!

14:48.939 --> 14:50.441
Sure, he's cute now.

14:50.524 --> 14:53.069
But when he's older,
he'll join the Fire Nation army.

14:53.360 --> 14:55.112
You won't think he's so cute then.

14:55.196 --> 14:56.989
He'll be a killer.

14:57.239 --> 14:59.575
Does that look like
the face of a killer to you?

15:01.786 --> 15:03.621
( SQUAWKING )

15:05.164 --> 15:06.540
A messenger hawk.

15:08.584 --> 15:10.544
AANG: It's from the Fire Nation governor.

15:11.087 --> 15:12.963
He thinks we kidnapped his son.

15:13.047 --> 15:15.091
So, he wants to make a trade.

15:15.591 --> 15:16.634
His son...

15:16.717 --> 15:18.135
For King Bumi!

15:28.145 --> 15:30.981
SOKKA: You realize
we're probably walking right into a trap.

15:31.107 --> 15:32.108
I don't think so.

15:32.441 --> 15:34.401
I'm sure the governor wants his son back

15:34.485 --> 15:35.903
as much as we want Bumi.

15:35.986 --> 15:37.071
It's a new day.

15:37.446 --> 15:39.115
I have a good feeling about this.

15:48.749 --> 15:51.001
Please tell me you're
here to kill me.

15:52.461 --> 15:53.796
( CHUCKLES )

15:53.879 --> 15:55.381
It's great to see you, Mai.

15:56.257 --> 15:58.634
I thought you ran off
and joined the circus.

15:58.717 --> 16:00.136
You said it was your calling.

16:00.511 --> 16:03.389
Well, Azula called a little louder.

16:03.722 --> 16:04.765
I have a mission,

16:04.849 --> 16:06.267
and I need you both.

16:06.350 --> 16:07.351
Count me in.

16:07.810 --> 16:09.854
Anything to get me
out of this place.

16:10.771 --> 16:12.189
GOVERNOR: I apologize.

16:12.857 --> 16:15.025
You've come to Omashu at a difficult time.

16:15.401 --> 16:17.027
At noon, we're making a trade

16:17.111 --> 16:19.446
with the resistance to get Tom-Tom back.

16:19.530 --> 16:22.575
Yes, I'm so sorry to
hear about your son.

16:22.658 --> 16:24.577
But, really, what did you expect

16:24.660 --> 16:27.329
by just letting all the citizens leave?

16:28.289 --> 16:30.416
My father has trusted you with this city,

16:30.499 --> 16:32.209
and you're making a mess of things.

16:32.293 --> 16:33.627
Forgive me, Princess.

16:34.211 --> 16:35.462
You stay here.

16:35.546 --> 16:37.131
Mai will handle the hostage trade

16:37.214 --> 16:39.216
so you don't have a chance to mess it up.

16:39.633 --> 16:41.302
AZULA: And there is no more Omashu.

16:41.385 --> 16:43.637
I am renaming it
in honor of my father.

16:43.762 --> 16:45.931
The city of New Ozai!

16:58.611 --> 16:59.612
( CHUCKLING )

17:01.447 --> 17:03.365
Hi, everybody!

17:05.951 --> 17:07.286
You brought my brother?

17:07.369 --> 17:08.495
AANG: He's here.

17:09.121 --> 17:10.539
We're ready to trade.

17:11.165 --> 17:13.375
I'm sorry, but a thought
just occurred to me.

17:13.459 --> 17:14.543
Do you mind?

17:14.627 --> 17:16.587
Of course not, Princess Azula.

17:16.670 --> 17:19.298
We're trading a two-year-old for a king―

17:19.381 --> 17:21.926
A powerful earthbending king.

17:22.801 --> 17:24.678
It just doesn't seem like a fair trade.

17:24.762 --> 17:25.763
Does it?

17:29.183 --> 17:30.184
You're right.

17:32.895 --> 17:34.146
The deal's off.

17:34.230 --> 17:35.397
Whoa!

17:36.023 --> 17:37.233
See you all later!

17:37.691 --> 17:39.193
( SNORT ) Ha ha ha.

17:39.693 --> 17:42.071
AANG: Bumi!

17:42.154 --> 17:43.572
( GRUNTS )

17:47.576 --> 17:48.577
( GRUNTS )

17:48.661 --> 17:50.079
The Avatar.

17:52.164 --> 17:53.958
My lucky day.

18:00.256 --> 18:02.132
Aang! Is that you?

18:02.216 --> 18:03.842
Where did you
come from?

18:04.218 --> 18:06.762
Hang on. We're gonna get you out of here.

18:14.645 --> 18:16.522
We've gotta get the baby out of here!

18:17.481 --> 18:19.108
Way ahead of you.

18:22.486 --> 18:23.821
( GRUNTING )

18:39.128 --> 18:40.129
( SCREAMS )

18:46.093 --> 18:48.512
Aang! Stop your blowing for a minute.

18:52.516 --> 18:53.517
( GROWLING )

18:53.642 --> 18:54.935
BUMI: Now hold on just a―

18:55.019 --> 18:56.645
Aagh!

19:12.119 --> 19:13.203
( LAUGHING )

19:13.287 --> 19:14.496
It's just like old times,

19:14.580 --> 19:15.581
Isn't it, Bumi?

19:15.664 --> 19:17.833
Aang, I need to talk to you!

19:17.916 --> 19:19.626
It's good to see you, too!

19:32.222 --> 19:33.223
Aagh!

19:50.074 --> 19:51.325
Phew!

19:52.868 --> 19:53.869
Aagh!

20:03.462 --> 20:04.463
( GRUNTS )

20:08.258 --> 20:10.386
( GRUNTING )

20:16.975 --> 20:19.228
How are you gonna fight
without your bending?

20:20.270 --> 20:21.397
( GASPS )

20:21.480 --> 20:22.564
( GRUNTS )

20:22.898 --> 20:23.941
I seem to manage!

20:27.152 --> 20:28.779
( SCREAMS )

20:31.532 --> 20:32.616
There's Aang!

20:32.699 --> 20:33.867
We can catch him!

20:38.872 --> 20:40.082
Hang on, Bumi!

20:40.165 --> 20:41.375
Our ride's here!

20:45.462 --> 20:46.547
( GRUNTING )

20:47.131 --> 20:48.465
Aang!

20:51.552 --> 20:52.803
Oof!

20:57.850 --> 20:58.851
( GRUNTS )

21:17.786 --> 21:18.871
You could earthbend...

21:19.246 --> 21:20.414
All along?!

21:20.539 --> 21:22.666
Well, they didn't cover my face.

21:23.542 --> 21:24.710
( GRUNTS )

21:26.753 --> 21:27.963
I don't understand.

21:28.046 --> 21:29.715
Why didn't you free yourself?

21:30.048 --> 21:32.259
Why did you surrender
when Omashu was invaded?

21:32.342 --> 21:34.261
What's the matter with you, Bumi?!

21:34.344 --> 21:35.846
Listen to me, Aang.

21:36.138 --> 21:38.474
There are options in fighting called jing.

21:38.557 --> 21:41.602
It's a choice of how
you direct your energy.

21:42.060 --> 21:44.146
I know! Positive jing
when you're attacking,

21:44.229 --> 21:46.190
and negative jing when you're retreating.

21:46.565 --> 21:49.276
And neutral jing, when you do nothing.

21:49.359 --> 21:51.111
There are three jings?

21:51.195 --> 21:53.238
Well, technically, there are 85.

21:53.322 --> 21:55.407
But let's just focus on the third.

21:55.824 --> 21:58.785
Neutral jing is the key
to earthbending.

21:58.869 --> 22:01.205
It involves listening and waiting

22:01.288 --> 22:03.582
for the right moment to strike.

22:03.916 --> 22:06.084
That's why you surrendered, isn't it?

22:06.168 --> 22:08.670
Yes, and it's why I can't leave now.

22:10.756 --> 22:13.800
I guess I need to find someone else
to teach me earthbending.

22:13.884 --> 22:15.385
Your teacher will be someone

22:15.469 --> 22:17.763
who has mastered neutral jing.

22:17.846 --> 22:19.264
You need to find someone

22:19.348 --> 22:22.976
who waits and listens before striking.

22:23.101 --> 22:24.269
-( COOING )
- Hey, Momo.

22:24.603 --> 22:27.147
Momo's mastered
a few jings himself.

22:27.773 --> 22:28.941
( SQUEALS )

22:29.024 --> 22:30.275
Good-bye, Aang.

22:30.359 --> 22:33.153
I'll see you when the time is right.

22:33.278 --> 22:35.489
( LAUGHING )

22:35.614 --> 22:38.158
( SNORTING )

22:42.329 --> 22:45.165
So, we're tracking down
your brother and uncle, huh?

22:45.249 --> 22:47.459
It'll be interesting seeing Zuko again,

22:47.543 --> 22:48.877
won't it, Mai?

22:49.670 --> 22:52.506
It's not just Zuko And Iroh anymore.

22:52.631 --> 22:54.716
We have a third target now.

23:00.556 --> 23:02.432
( COOING )

23:05.185 --> 23:06.770
( GURGLING )

23:06.853 --> 23:07.980
( GASPS )

23:08.105 --> 23:09.940
Tom-tom!
